.\" ###### Setup ############################################################
.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt subnetcalc 1
.Os subnetcalc
.\" ###### Name #############################################################
.Sh NAME
.Nm subnetcalc
.Nd IPv4/IPv6 Subnet Calculator
.\" ###### Synopsis #########################################################
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm subnetcalc
.No { Ar address/prefix | Ar address/netmask | Ar address Ar prefix | Ar address Ar netmask No }
.br
.Op Fl F Ar text|json|yaml|xml | Fl \-format Ar text|json|yaml|xml
.br
.Op Fl u | Fl \-uniquelocal
.Op Fl U | Fl \-uniquelocalhq
.br
.Op Fl n | Fl \-noreverselookup
.br
.Op Fl g | Fl \-nogeoiplookup
.br
.Op Fl c | Fl \-nocolour | Fl \-nocolor
.br
.Op Fl 4 | Fl \-ipv4
.Op Fl 6 | Fl \-ipv6
.Nm subnetcalc
.Op Fl h | Fl \-help
.Nm subnetcalc
.Op Fl v | Fl \-version
.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm subnetcalc
is an IPv4/IPv6 subnet address calculator.
For a given IPv4 or IPv6 address and netmask or prefix length, it calculates network address, broadcast address, maximum number of hosts and host address range.
Also, it prints the addresses in binary format for better understandability.
Furthermore, it prints useful information on specific address types (e.g., type, scope, interface ID, etc.).
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following arguments and options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ar address
The IP address. If a hostname is provided here, the program attempts to resolve the hostname via a DNS server, and the first returned address is used. Internationalized Domain Names (IDN) are supported.
.It Ar netmask
The netmask.
.It Ar prefix
The prefix length (0\-32 for IPv4; 0\-128 for IPv6).
.It Fl F Ar text|json|yaml|xml | Fl \-format Ar text|json|yaml|xml
Sets the output format. Supported formats are
.Cm text
(default human\-readable formatted output),
.Cm json
(JavaScript Object Notation),
.Cm yaml
(YAML Ain't Markup Language), and
.Cm xml
(Extensible Markup Language).
.It Fl u | Fl \-uniquelocal
Given an IPv6 address, the first 48 bits of the address are replaced by a randomly chosen IPv6 Unique Local prefix in
.Cm fc00::/7
(see also RFC 4193). On Unix systems,
.Pa /dev/urandom
is used for random number generation.
.It Fl U | Fl \-uniquelocalhq
Like
.Fl \-uniquelocal ,
but using
.Pa /dev/random
instead on Unix systems for highest\-quality random number generation. On other systems, this option is equal to
.Fl \-uniquelocal .
Note that reading from
.Pa /dev/random
may take some time. You can speed up this process by delivering random input, e.g., by pressing keys or moving the mouse.
.It Fl n | Fl \-noreverselookup
Turns reverse DNS lookup off.
.It Fl g | Fl \-nogeoiplookup
Turns GeoIP lookup off.
.It Fl c | Fl \-nocolour | Fl \-nocolor
Turns colourised output off.
.It Fl 4 | Fl \-ipv4
Forces hostname resolution to IPv4 addresses.
.It Fl 6 | Fl \-ipv6
Forces hostname resolution to IPv6 addresses.
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints the program's command\-line parameters and exits.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints the program version and exits.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -bullet
.It
subnetcalc \-v
.It
subnetcalc 132.252.250.0 255.255.255.0
.It
subnetcalc 132.252.250.0/255.255.255.0 \-\-nocolor
.It
subnetcalc 132.252.250.0 24
.It
subnetcalc 132.252.250.0/24 \-\-nocolour
.It
subnetcalc fe80::2f0b:a04e:15c2:bc68 64
.It
subnetcalc fe80::2f0b:a04e:15c2:bc68%wlp4s0 64
.It
subnetcalc fec0:2345:6789:1111:221:6aff:fe0b:2674 56
.It
subnetcalc 2a00:1450:8007::69 64
.It
subnetcalc ff08::1:2:3
.It
subnetcalc 131.220.6.5/24
.It
subnetcalc 132.252.181.87 \-n
.It
subnetcalc www.iem.uni\-due.de 24
.It
subnetcalc www.six.heise.de
.It
subnetcalc www.heise.de \-4 24
.It
subnetcalc www.nntb.no \-6 64
.It
subnetcalc fd00:: 64 \-\-uniquelocal
.It
subnetcalc fd00::9876:256:7bff:fe1b:3255 56 \-\-uniquelocalhq
.It
subnetcalc 192.168.1.1/24 \-F json
.It
subnetcalc 192.168.1.1/24 \-F yaml
.It
subnetcalc 2001:db8::1/64 \-F xml
.It
subnetcalc www.heise.de \-\-format yaml
.It
subnetcalc düsseldorf.de 28
.It
subnetcalc www.köln.de
.It
subnetcalc räksmörgås.josefsson.org 24
.It
subnetcalc xn\-\-smrgstrta\-82ac2r.xn\-\-domne\-ira.example 26
.It
subnetcalc smörgåstårta.domäne.example 255.255.255.240
.El
